{"uid":"6517dc2e4f7940e","name":"test_review_verdict_writes_the_adjudication_into_the_run_dir_never_the_workspace_tree","fullName":"tests.test_petitions#test_review_verdict_writes_the_adjudication_into_the_run_dir_never_the_workspace_tree","historyId":"994d27dccffe0915e58c4a55c9b17766","time":{"start":1791925268199,"stop":1791925268252,"duration":53},"description":"Task 065 (requirement N.6, #150): `_write_back_petition_adjudications`\n    now threads `run=self.run` into `petitions.write_back_petition_\n    adjudication`, so the CONFIRMED/REFUTED marker for an obligation this\n    RUN itself filed (through the run-dir `file_worker_petition` path)\n    lands in `sup.run.petitions_file` -- never a `*-petitions.md` file\n    under the workspace tree, and never a git commit against the\n    workspace (there is nothing there for `_commit_petition_writeback` to\n    add). #150 (the historical multi-wave-glob duplicate-obligation bug)\n    stays CLOSED -- unrelated to where this writes.\n\n    Retires the four `_review_verdict`-driven tests this replaces\n    (`test_review_verdict_writes_the_adjudication_into_the_tracked_file`,\n    `test_a_clean_workspace_commits_the_writeback_with_the_run_identity`,\n    `test_a_dirty_workspace_defers_the_commit_to_the_next_task_boundary`,\n    `test_a_non_git_workspace_still_gets_the_write`): each pinned the\n    write-back landing IN the workspace tree and being committed there,\n    which requirement N.6 retires outright. Their surviving cover is this\n    test (the run-dir write-back itself) plus `test_petition_adjudications_\n    run_scope.py`'s existing suite (the JSON store this same run-dir\n    write-back sits beside) and `test_a_workspace_filed_petitions_\n    adjudication_write_back_is_a_noop_against_the_tree` below (a petition\n    filed the OLD way, before this obligation's own filing moved).\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 065 (requirement N.6, #150): <code>_write_back_petition_adjudications</code><br />\nnow threads <code>run=self.run</code> into <code>petitions.write_back_petition_ adjudication</code>, so the CONFIRMED/REFUTED marker for an obligation this<br />\nRUN itself filed (through the run-dir <code>file_worker_petition</code> path)<br />\nlands in <code>sup.run.petitions_file</code> -- never a <code>*-petitions.md</code> file<br />\nunder the workspace tree, and never a git commit against the<br />\nworkspace (there is nothing there for <code>_commit_petition_writeback</code> to<br />\nadd). #150 (the historical multi-wave-glob duplicate-obligation bug)<br />\nstays CLOSED -- unrelated to where this writes.</p>\n<pre><code>Retires the four `_review_verdict`-driven tests this replaces\n(`test_review_verdict_writes_the_adjudication_into_the_tracked_file`,\n`test_a_clean_workspace_commits_the_writeback_with_the_run_identity`,\n`test_a_dirty_workspace_defers_the_commit_to_the_next_task_boundary`,\n`test_a_non_git_workspace_still_gets_the_write`): each pinned the\nwrite-back landing IN the workspace tree and being committed there,\nwhich requirement N.6 retires outright. Their surviving cover is this\ntest (the run-dir write-back itself) plus `test_petition_adjudications_\nrun_scope.py`'s existing suite (the JSON store this same run-dir\nwrite-back sits beside) and `test_a_workspace_filed_petitions_\nadjudication_write_back_is_a_noop_against_the_tree` below (a petition\nfiled the OLD way, before this obligation's own filing moved).\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791925216356,"stop":1791925216356,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791925216356,"stop":1791925216357,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attach